#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618044 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11d8dbdf-4135-5d69-850b-228a773a98a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/55/557488774f01166c4a636c231e34bb2f1a0aba8404fd90c64eb7d598c7616460.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618018} {:answer/id #uuid "330b35c0-736a-5524-a023-d4dccad04b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f6522538bf8ea1b4515e5a043c58a693b8e037c9a8b7b4385239d4c7e008d7f9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618022} {:answer/id #uuid "608d457a-7362-582d-9c69-c1e1bf615ba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d2/d28207116cba4547332a09c1413449de39713759bbb36e927c3929951e2d9dd1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618029} {:answer/id #uuid "925fcf8e-4efc-5126-8e4c-44e990e2d7e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b6/b6d9743048b7b3ef7a0c26ac21df36c45e2b3a044fe738b875ac2883fb62d5ea.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618036} {:answer/id #uuid "c0fd4f99-6a82-59dd-bf9a-7a3a861fd422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/13fab6a82cf80f89436ace5c1a4335e272460ea8aa661d75a6f5aeaa74624471.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "925fcf8e-4efc-5126-8e4c-44e990e2d7e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b6/b6d9743048b7b3ef7a0c26ac21df36c45e2b3a044fe738b875ac2883fb62d5ea.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618036} :answer-field/id #uuid "077e5e71-a36d-561c-bbad-6a2c5003626d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "df3d7c84-11c3-5403-85e8-f6747a9bed57" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=-x+2.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-x+2.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=-(0)+2=2,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-(1)+2=1,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=-(2)+2=0,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-(3)+2=-1.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/c3/c37a098fd2295afed0d1793286f0d36f7d2bd452e25c3df2b754c6ee50621a1f.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-x+2.$\n\n![](images/b6/b6d9743048b7b3ef7a0c26ac21df36c45e2b3a044fe738b875ac2883fb62d5ea.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618047 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10806a24-37e5-58cd-b151-e514d9429362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1d0b329d967131adcc50f00d0a130095bf6854d86d7caeb21c5c54a593ba86c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618017} {:answer/id #uuid "4e494b5c-95fd-5842-a6f5-52d711a8abe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/35/351f1223ae000576aa8017fcccc4d234d6ebab0b511e94523e4e75571ac9d28f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618026} {:answer/id #uuid "7219d2ee-cb12-5fdc-8607-c34ed392a7d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/34e908221ed8aa5608732cc28b19a23cb42ef2ff1ae18cf8091648657cab795b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618031} {:answer/id #uuid "ca507f1a-b726-5924-8221-50dbf2351573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cd/cd48bdb35121392b12984b4f2e7e5ee2adc8950c316d86e7942cdcb1309cb441.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618041} {:answer/id #uuid "e821359a-818e-5228-8e9f-91555a864abc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4cdcb21d8b43f4f6014b302e03343712978e34c8c9ac213ee1b9f85d9171e785.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7219d2ee-cb12-5fdc-8607-c34ed392a7d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/34e908221ed8aa5608732cc28b19a23cb42ef2ff1ae18cf8091648657cab795b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618031} :answer-field/id #uuid "e034452b-d7bf-55d5-b565-01b2feeb9a5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f417ba21-a2aa-5ffc-abae-dadd4a903d42" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=2x-2.$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=2x-2.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=2(2)-2=2,$\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=2(3)-2=4,$\n\n- if $x=4$ then $y=2(4)-2=6,$ and\n\n- if $x=5$ then $y=2(5)-2=8.$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/f3/f380135b711cadd50e16ad9e1121c558b205d11536947f1adbc8e767f015f068.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=2x-2.$\n\n![](images/34/34e908221ed8aa5608732cc28b19a23cb42ef2ff1ae18cf8091648657cab795b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186620824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097f5ddb-42a0-50bb-b845-cb4d9e479604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619974} {:answer/id #uuid "4d1787a2-b9b6-5a0c-be24-248c54804487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620173} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd8235d-86e9-5a08-97f3-d7ec1735ad4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620207} {:answer/id #uuid "912bd962-fcee-5f4d-89e7-311ac8bc8abf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6,12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620354} {:answer/id #uuid "f04b13d4-f291-5a54-a1e3-01f656e1a0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "097f5ddb-42a0-50bb-b845-cb4d9e479604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186619974} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f6f1dc4-1d03-59e8-9f3c-890ae207a2c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1ba4640e-a0c2-5e1b-8816-6d483fc28a4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-19784" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨2,0,x⟩$, $b=⟨3,2,x⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{61}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & x \\\\ 3 & 2 & x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}0 & x \\\\ 2 & x\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & x \\\\ 3 & x\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(0-2x)i-(2x-3x)j+(4-0)k \\\\  & =⟨-2x,x,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-2x)^{2}+{x}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{x}^{2}+16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{61} \\\\ \\sqrt{5{x}^{2}+16} & =\\sqrt{61} \\\\ 5{x}^{2}+16 & =61 \\\\ 5{x}^{2} & =45 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=\\pm 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186620854 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ac51d43-c404-5c07-a099-4936d5b5b0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ac51d43-c404-5c07-a099-4936d5b5b0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620122} :answer-field/id #uuid "047adb9b-443f-5f0b-afaf-9f3f1041c3ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620654} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de44f899-a20f-5a4a-b9ab-33ca776c18a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620558}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de44f899-a20f-5a4a-b9ab-33ca776c18a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620558} :answer-field/id #uuid "08d81bba-b208-514a-8abe-99c0a6c03f7f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "743e3bd8-5ebd-55b3-b55c-3c9f7eb86fc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-275293" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨x,3,6⟩,$ $b=⟨2,1,2⟩$ and $|\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{80}.$ Then, in **ascending order**, the possible values of $x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ x & 3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}x & 6 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}x & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(6-6)i-(2x-12)j+(x-6)k \\\\  & =⟨0,12-2x,x-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(12-2x)^{2}+(x-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144-48x+4{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}-12x+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{x}^{2}-60x+180}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\ \\sqrt{5{x}^{2}-50x+180} & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-60x+180 & =80 \\\\ 5{x}^{2}-60x+100 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-12x+20 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)(x-10) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $x=2,$ $x=10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186620984 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271409d5-4217-5c85-b07c-9e0df003989b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620978} {:answer/id #uuid "362293ce-6960-5bec-bd1d-91d950c62c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620979} {:answer/id #uuid "5442b9e8-2d41-5f44-aa1b-5bf84a779714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620980} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1008cf-16e7-59e5-9723-0377df844c92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620982} {:answer/id #uuid "cf9bd0de-8993-53c8-b29e-a2a030396acb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e1008cf-16e7-59e5-9723-0377df844c92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620982} :answer-field/id #uuid "8826ac9f-6e72-51e7-9d14-5ca172f0524c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f96934b1-b807-5be7-b577-eeccabeded8d" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(2 x^{2} - 3)^{4},$ find the slope at the point $(1,1)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nWe use the chain rule to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{4},\\,g=2 x^{2} - 3\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4g^{3},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=4 x.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=4g^{3}\\cdot (4 x) \\\\  &=16 x(2 x^{2} - 3)^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line at the point where $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|_{x=1} &=[16 x(2 x^{2} - 3)^{3}]|_{x=1} \\\\  &=16 (1)(2 (1)^{2} - 3)^{3} \\\\  &=-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186620993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13a8d4ef-fbda-549e-95c0-07466fb9ef92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620987} {:answer/id #uuid "52c8ebaa-290e-5710-b83c-8fba8f52be37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620992} {:answer/id #uuid "91e0b753-5cf9-5d35-bb55-6742658c6c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620996} {:answer/id #uuid "9414db0b-bcf9-5ba0-b2f3-875988418075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620997} {:answer/id #uuid "f7cc6e1a-d443-5bf8-9a5f-bb367ab98026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91e0b753-5cf9-5d35-bb55-6742658c6c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620996} :answer-field/id #uuid "50244b30-dd7d-5b8a-a15a-82736c084032" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "60135066-889b-5619-94cd-26f06014ccda" :question/problem "![](images/51/5126c74f997dc78e8a14e444b16999781f57f9a3f09db40fd185592195f2cb77.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-2x-4$?" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-1,-3)$, $B(-2,3)$, $C(-3,2)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-1,-3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-4 \\\\ (-3) &= -2(-1)-4 \\\\ -3 &= -2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-2,3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-4 \\\\ (3) &= -2(-2)-4 \\\\ 3 &= 0 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-3,2)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-4 \\\\ (2) &= -2(-3)-4 \\\\ 2 &= 2 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $B$ do not lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186620998 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1de87454-44d5-592b-afbd-abbc29ab37cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620988} {:answer/id #uuid "d8aa8be2-d9e7-5b3f-9f88-0dd54a0ee367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621002} {:answer/id #uuid "d9424749-99d7-5d09-932c-d3e0dc9dd758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621003} {:answer/id #uuid "da81ccc9-aadc-5ed2-b60c-654b19e9b8b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621004} {:answer/id #uuid "ecc1b92c-0a5f-530b-a637-fb69aa728de4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8aa8be2-d9e7-5b3f-9f88-0dd54a0ee367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621002} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2f454d2-62fd-53e1-bb8b-2b01f65da1e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620999}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9cff71c7-5618-5c9d-9553-1246ce19e5dc" :question/problem "![](images/58/5826c4d6340af4a652a2bac5260c51e6b6e9ecf95478627be1705f0cf5b1d727.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-3x+4$." :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,3)$, $B(3,-5)$, $C(2,-2)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x+4 \\\\ (3) &= -3(0)+4 \\\\ 3 &= 4 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(3,-5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x+4 \\\\ (-5) &= -3(3)+4 \\\\ -5 &= -5 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-2)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x+4 \\\\ (-2) &= -3(2)+4 \\\\ -2 &= -2 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $A$ does not lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186621001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e365f58-7e8d-5fba-9a05-794b476f2607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620986} {:answer/id #uuid "28287f65-d177-56b1-a077-c46b908c0076" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620989} {:answer/id #uuid "311bc49c-0f4c-5020-b77b-4bf867c56505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620990} {:answer/id #uuid "7fc28b9d-ee8f-5780-ae34-917296a092c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620994} {:answer/id #uuid "c1fea169-9544-5064-82ea-4be72bde2a4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e365f58-7e8d-5fba-9a05-794b476f2607" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620986} :answer-field/id #uuid "8629f778-4aaf-55e5-b0a1-4991e5585b5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ce9f03f6-0338-5b5e-a4a2-b3cff5f6d12f" :question/problem "![](images/11/11423dab0f796e898be878520cf136c1130273aa66f01639b37e5f949785d6d6.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-2x+2$." :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,6)$, $B(2,-4)$, $C(-1,7)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+2 \\\\ (6) &= -2(-2)+2 \\\\ 6 &= 6 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(2,-4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+2 \\\\ (-4) &= -2(2)+2 \\\\ -4 &= -2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-1,7)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+2 \\\\ (7) &= -2(-1)+2 \\\\ 7 &= 4 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $B$ and $C$ do not lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186621048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05e2ecf4-254e-5383-a70d-fb1403c679f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4cba6447959ecaba1b44d3f0b2cca81105f5089f40cba98a986fc961b3a9e689.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621044} {:answer/id #uuid "098ce027-9fd6-5e7c-b906-790d0d48803d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8e/8e7fd52bc7671a54fcb6d16cf845624bd47b6691788e3fbd64d9e46b1f989374.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621045} {:answer/id #uuid "6653485a-17ee-5818-8886-4a69cf98a3cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a0/a04db1eb7a6095f82e34950a9ec2a7cc212d1dd486081010beaae4df81b6f536.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621053} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6305d3-942d-5ad3-818f-2a0b11f9f226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fc/fcba7a3ff13867701f1b58fe92ed7df2cc0024f56c2a1fcfb0e1b2c409bba733.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621058} {:answer/id #uuid "d52188e6-314f-5b65-b1c2-63fb4e5310a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4ca1fa078f7f6d8136a030e7ec44adf796ed06481ff3aaafbefe74d88a5a6c15.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621063}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d52188e6-314f-5b65-b1c2-63fb4e5310a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4ca1fa078f7f6d8136a030e7ec44adf796ed06481ff3aaafbefe74d88a5a6c15.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621063} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f689ee7-6c07-5a02-80d0-a7c8ef88fdf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "146e6c91-2556-5cd3-8d0a-3b7252d4021a" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=-4x-2.$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-4x-2.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-4(1)-2=-6,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=-4(2)-2=-10,$\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-4(3)-2=-14,$ and\n\n- if $x=4$ then $y=-4(4)-2=-18.$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-10$ | $-14$ | $-18$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/d2/d2be7541030a65f678da5971d797579a0c6081cec346be25a879116fdbd6f72c.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-4x-2.$\n\n![](images/4c/4ca1fa078f7f6d8136a030e7ec44adf796ed06481ff3aaafbefe74d88a5a6c15.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186621050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0343c080-291d-5cfe-ac2f-58c9246e28db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/22/22709bad1a7cb6b49244b434a429cdb9886cfd005eafa6be4291e11b49e69232.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621043} {:answer/id #uuid "10528f4e-88cf-5c72-ae83-0f6f0cb12a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/01/012984a957594c22178d15b5505231507b80efd92e68e294e6afecd5a9cca9bf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621047} {:answer/id #uuid "7adbcd1d-ef6b-5dd2-b1bd-5dee3f29f729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/04/04ef1ab2a7d66ec11b7dcd0cffd648bd8c73d639d4d2dafa0930a8743ea9e1e5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621055} {:answer/id #uuid "90f521ac-5159-546b-b8d6-a7797205016f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8ff7d16f47b69a9fa08edc07e28212df35a95bdea62f2326b5ee38caf143c7c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621059} {:answer/id #uuid "9ecd31e4-0600-53c5-b04d-33617bac25cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2d/2d388d5b2240d45b1a79abe1c4c3e04002a515f613ca87e2ab4e5b131b26cbcb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ecd31e4-0600-53c5-b04d-33617bac25cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2d/2d388d5b2240d45b1a79abe1c4c3e04002a515f613ca87e2ab4e5b131b26cbcb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621061} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c49dc68-f4bd-5e18-b602-18507687c6f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3208e1f5-ac27-5545-8473-0258b81d1323" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=-3x-2.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-3x-2.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=-3(0)-2=-2,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-3(1)-2=-5,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=-3(2)-2=-8,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-3(3)-2=-11.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $-5$ | $-8$ | $-11$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/51/51adf104900ef3b01fe71d15aa250ed872805fbbaecf7a0382a6ce6f2f1c603f.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-3x-2.$\n\n![](images/2d/2d388d5b2240d45b1a79abe1c4c3e04002a515f613ca87e2ab4e5b131b26cbcb.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186621057 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f9071f1-26d3-5342-a732-80f05bd5998b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8b/8bedb6981887e247c7b03296e5d636c91e01ff2a5d7b29adba48fd9028badc91.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621046} {:answer/id #uuid "209135c3-a461-57f5-a90b-c40c99d00530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bf/bf22926eadb33f5366fca44ef8422a31ce5f66fb5fe7e2cf8c84b1a1a6b2d1ca.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621049} {:answer/id #uuid "3f03b99e-c2b2-565d-b651-111f01960afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/493363ba9b516b87855da69fcf796f7d9b5ff6cb74548c08e82138ae84040e8b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621051} {:answer/id #uuid "6eb597ab-4c9a-5db2-8d21-4d381c60e15d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/03/03fa8418a4c66a98c057c32e747e7c1bc42b0cced96ab9b27c65c4f2af0982c2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621054} {:answer/id #uuid "a9c99982-b294-5730-ba34-9fd70257941a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8a/8a81f5512e2d7e43bfcce3e6f6b97ce0742faf3cccc6b10e8ee2afe7e4b24c71.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f03b99e-c2b2-565d-b651-111f01960afe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/493363ba9b516b87855da69fcf796f7d9b5ff6cb74548c08e82138ae84040e8b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621051} :answer-field/id #uuid "98591e94-7cc3-5855-9415-d9799c597423" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186621060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89235afd-0c9c-5b7c-ad75-401b320b6e62" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=-4x+5.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-4x+5.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=-4(0)+5=5,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-4(1)+5=1,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=-4(2)+5=-3,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-4(3)+5=-7.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $1$ | $-3$ | $-7$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/b9/b98f86cec2f28d1eecf50c09eb625837cb8a0a6cbdd83960ffd4ffd34ff9df9d.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-4x+5.$\n\n![](images/49/493363ba9b516b87855da69fcf796f7d9b5ff6cb74548c08e82138ae84040e8b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622064 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "286a02cd-f6de-5e5b-acb1-c9083a17bc46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622063} {:answer/id #uuid "765741c3-5de0-59c4-9f60-1e78031b0d38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622072} {:answer/id #uuid "add6a0f8-34a2-5c05-907a-a669cb0d7ac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622082} {:answer/id #uuid "c4d7cfa0-aadc-524e-b4bd-a9fdb1bb1dc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622084} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f4a531-3cfd-5751-94b4-e89883e71e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "add6a0f8-34a2-5c05-907a-a669cb0d7ac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622082} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f59d994-fd30-578f-888f-23350a7cd4db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622070}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2b256ba2-b92e-5837-988d-ac572b89d2ce" :question/problem "![](images/92/925bbc9a27faad62d5672c40bfe15ae47d3daed9dca2c307aea97f8d59742f6d.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y-\\frac{2}{3}x=-3$\n\nII. $- \\frac{3}{2}y+x=\\frac{9}{2}$\n\nIII. $y=\\frac{2}{3}x-4$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-3)$ and $(3,-1)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/2f/2fd4e2ba95ed99c626122fb351b6df0d7bf78dd750a565d84e135689062007c0.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y-\\frac{2}{3}x=-3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(3,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)-\\frac{2}{3}(0) &=-3 \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1)-\\frac{2}{3}(3) &=-3 \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y-\\frac{2}{3}x=-3$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $- \\frac{3}{2}y+x=\\frac{9}{2}.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(3,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- \\frac{3}{2}(-3)+(0) &=\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} &=\\frac{9}{2}\\,\\checkmark \\\\ - \\frac{3}{2}(-1)+(3) &=\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{2} &=\\frac{9}{2}\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $- \\frac{3}{2}y+x=\\frac{9}{2}$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=\\frac{2}{3}x-4.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3) &=\\frac{2}{3}(0)-4 \\\\ -3 &=-4\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{2}{3}x-4$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the equations that represented the line in the graph were $y-\\frac{2}{3}x=-3$, $- \\frac{3}{2}y+x=\\frac{9}{2}$, corresponding to I, II. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a7cf8b-3e26-524a-9654-aee7e100e7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622059} {:answer/id #uuid "06ac5fd2-b7c3-5435-b39d-7b6bbbd8a96a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622061} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa043ec-2e50-5c11-bbc7-034cae3cc3cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622086} {:answer/id #uuid "ea24025f-142e-5b43-afb7-f17a2d3872fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622088} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a36f15-6c33-5707-8455-6761abde7c99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfa043ec-2e50-5c11-bbc7-034cae3cc3cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622086} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac3ecc4b-7f4b-5443-9a26-fc05cd6d3a6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622081}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "302ad948-04cd-5352-96a4-47fb22f30dc7" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d33c96c388c19a4bd5b9c575d75a5ab1c4d53071b8279fd9d5eae60c6dbed8a4.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y=-2x-2$\n\nII. $y=-2+\\frac{1}{2}x$\n\nIII. $y+\\frac{1}{2}x=-2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-2)$ and $(2,-3)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/4e/4e51f973e8c91836e7b3d762e175e3941b45dcc10dd805984c743bec90b456b0.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=-2x-2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-2)$ and $B(2,-3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2) &=-2(0)-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-3) &=-2(2)-2 \\\\ -3 &=-6\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-2x-2$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=-2+\\frac{1}{2}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-2)$ and $B(2,-3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2) &=-2+\\frac{1}{2}(0) \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-3) &=-2+\\frac{1}{2}(2) \\\\ -3 &=-1\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-2+\\frac{1}{2}x$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y+\\frac{1}{2}x=-2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-2)$ and $B(2,-3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)+\\frac{1}{2}(0) &=-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-3)+\\frac{1}{2}(2) &=-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y+\\frac{1}{2}x=-2$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the equations that represented the line in the graph were $y+\\frac{1}{2}x=-2$, corresponding to III. Therefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622069 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68b11114-c852-5f90-add2-c1b2cd078dfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622071} {:answer/id #uuid "7d8944bd-b5e5-5628-9a25-cca9dc719ad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622073} {:answer/id #uuid "91dcfe58-e66a-5592-9183-435e8ff56538" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622076} {:answer/id #uuid "a40f15b3-3e87-59c7-b54b-3f6deca3a32f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622080} {:answer/id #uuid "b78684c6-6e60-5534-b3b9-091e205e4a01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a40f15b3-3e87-59c7-b54b-3f6deca3a32f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622080} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c5c304a-0288-5905-8624-e98f4fc32c2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "56e9599c-db83-5c89-a2a1-4cd50cdf6b50" :question/problem "![](images/75/7542265fbd9974f33a1d4e9124dbd2df61eb15ed30f61a3399abe8996550a6bb.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y=\\frac{3}{2}x-1$\n\nII. $y=0+\\frac{3}{2}x$\n\nIII. $y-\\frac{3}{2}x=-1$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-1)$ and $(2,2)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/ca/ca567dbc547d11cf337835ed7d7213a3e2c5e9b513fce544f7bcad21177ddacc.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=\\frac{3}{2}x-1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,2)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) &=\\frac{3}{2}(0)-1 \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (2) &=\\frac{3}{2}(2)-1 \\\\ 2 &=2\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{3}{2}x-1$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=0+\\frac{3}{2}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) &=0+\\frac{3}{2}(0) \\\\ -1 &=0\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=0+\\frac{3}{2}x$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y-\\frac{3}{2}x=-1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,2)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)-\\frac{3}{2}(0) &=-1 \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (2)-\\frac{3}{2}(2) &=-1 \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y-\\frac{3}{2}x=-1$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the equations that represented the line in the graph were $y=\\frac{3}{2}x-1$, $y-\\frac{3}{2}x=-1$, corresponding to I, III. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622075 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e8d321-fcdf-5fe4-97b8-7f4104b03c98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622062} {:answer/id #uuid "3b1d6497-6037-5487-8d9f-50b3feeeaa0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622066} {:answer/id #uuid "4b42fe51-c446-509f-a323-5716658989a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622067} {:answer/id #uuid "9d9f7336-7652-557a-8e51-ee22ec0310a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622079} {:answer/id #uuid "fc70e23d-7e13-5937-a62d-1c45fc588ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc70e23d-7e13-5937-a62d-1c45fc588ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622093} :answer-field/id #uuid "055aee5b-f541-50be-8f9c-92d21917b842" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622060}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8701ee8f-1d0d-5716-b325-f7d7f4cb51ba" :question/problem "![](images/40/40b5efdcecdc520292c5f5be9047b061b3eb5da2b869be81397b26aed8a6d620.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y+\\frac{3}{2}x=3$\n\nII. $\\frac{3}{2}y+x=3$\n\nIII. $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x+2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,2)$ and $(2,-1)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/83/83f23046b24dcdcfee122662efddc944303865a368fd3fb54eca005fcb631fe7.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y+\\frac{3}{2}x=3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,2)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)+\\frac{3}{2}(0) &=3 \\\\ 2 &=3\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y+\\frac{3}{2}x=3$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $\\frac{3}{2}y+x=3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,2)$ and $B(2,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}(2)+(0) &=3 \\\\ 3 &=3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}(-1)+(2) &=3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} &=3\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{3}{2}y+x=3$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x+2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,2)$ and $B(2,-1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2) &=- \\frac{3}{2}(0)+2 \\\\ 2 &=2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-1) &=- \\frac{3}{2}(2)+2 \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x+2$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the equations that represented the line in the graph were $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x+2$, corresponding to III. Therefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5111c810-e05c-5b8c-9c42-b5ae9575b283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622068} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff31496-6469-5a07-8a8a-94a7e14eb5d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622074} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9d7601-1576-58d3-935c-1af9e9738ea4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622085} {:answer/id #uuid "f642144e-5467-58e9-acda-e20ea15484db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622091} {:answer/id #uuid "f69416e7-8d3d-5c45-ab57-b2483d2a2c0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5111c810-e05c-5b8c-9c42-b5ae9575b283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622068} :answer-field/id #uuid "99ad1dfa-54a1-5806-8ed2-5259802ae15f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ef670b10-7877-5dbc-93c6-94be458d86fd" :question/problem "![](images/97/971525a7902dac13a95d27a5a749888588f833f6d00c8eb666b11ed3fd723df9.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x-3$\n\nII. $y=-3+\\frac{2}{3}x$\n\nIII. $y+\\frac{2}{3}x=-3$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-3)$ and $(3,-5)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/b6/b66a54a81055f919d8c5f375ffae2c8e7fc4e4a5ecd14ba2b405c956614e7884.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x-3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(3,-5)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3) &=- \\frac{3}{2}(0)-3 \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-5) &=- \\frac{3}{2}(3)-3 \\\\ -5 &=- \\frac{15}{2}\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=- \\frac{3}{2}x-3$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=-3+\\frac{2}{3}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(3,-5)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3) &=-3+\\frac{2}{3}(0) \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-5) &=-3+\\frac{2}{3}(3) \\\\ -5 &=-1\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-3+\\frac{2}{3}x$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y+\\frac{2}{3}x=-3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(3,-5)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)+\\frac{2}{3}(0) &=-3 \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-5)+\\frac{2}{3}(3) &=-3 \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y+\\frac{2}{3}x=-3$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the equations that represented the line in the graph were $y+\\frac{2}{3}x=-3$, corresponding to III. Therefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622116 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4efa5af9-551e-546c-95c8-5d8aff25dfd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/15/15b20c37317414d4d531c99a1a3c34ea73d20ad3f526f63dea4aaea3be5c6518.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622124} {:answer/id #uuid "73c37d57-50c2-58f6-8f5f-ce8ea20d989b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/69/696b0f0b6c1f4f0257c7dcd754afdf63f95a83f4eeaf774afbc0347261ac7624.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622130} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f90278-a10e-5469-bb1f-626562b832b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e6/e66f5fea8b38cfc0fe9c46b18cc9f7d3a3a3d42a156c061ba53d06b293989ad9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622138} {:answer/id #uuid "efbaf866-899e-5a9f-b6ec-6ee0b6a4922d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d4c51cb0d3134283fe3a0f9fc9217136b595fe8b53f1655670a8fcdee75728e2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622144} {:answer/id #uuid "f48452e0-3b5e-57a0-8602-74be3e4387f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3e/3ebc10488aeec3d18b2f3e26f6504095e8338f10cb43d4e1a7b9586693c3f4f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73c37d57-50c2-58f6-8f5f-ce8ea20d989b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/69/696b0f0b6c1f4f0257c7dcd754afdf63f95a83f4eeaf774afbc0347261ac7624.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622130} :answer-field/id #uuid "b01cf34d-92fd-5d9e-94af-f3f6e6918682" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622137}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33780efb-3071-505b-ab92-4670e3020530" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y=-5-2x?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5-2x \\\\  & =-5-2(0) \\\\  & =-5-0 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,-5).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5-2x \\\\  & =-5-2(-2) \\\\  & =-5+4 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(-2,-1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-5-2x.$\n\n![](images/7c/7c1acc4c8a5aaf32eca945aabdda84f45fe35b62065c290dcdf75198bdf0f073.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23295da7-f025-5f58-bd6d-cbb893f731a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0a/0a2299c50f4697d6f548b9820fca69b5556fe031b3d363c07b94d6fe56844b2f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622113} {:answer/id #uuid "34cbd739-7c26-5a09-8e0f-f76406728c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/77/77d0ec38e520cf54a0f777813c350bae00c04e716e41a8a851ab69c5196cd785.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622117} {:answer/id #uuid "3eaf2d64-9f71-5c51-abc7-cd62debc2de6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/58/584308913552409f5a13552dfc5ababc6befe157d3f034c530bda2811e7b830d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622121} {:answer/id #uuid "6b379dee-4ed1-5e16-98be-cd7c1402015f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/69/696b0f0b6c1f4f0257c7dcd754afdf63f95a83f4eeaf774afbc0347261ac7624.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622127} {:answer/id #uuid "c656582c-29fd-5177-9e0c-22796bfbaad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d4c51cb0d3134283fe3a0f9fc9217136b595fe8b53f1655670a8fcdee75728e2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23295da7-f025-5f58-bd6d-cbb893f731a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0a/0a2299c50f4697d6f548b9820fca69b5556fe031b3d363c07b94d6fe56844b2f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622113} :answer-field/id #uuid "353c7e35-dc71-53c1-a7fa-5904b9a3be0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "603439df-1330-5adc-a8eb-fe5f271f6dc9" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y=2x-5?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x-5 \\\\  & =2(0)-5 \\\\  & =0-5 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,-5).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=-2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x-5 \\\\  & =2(-2)-5 \\\\  & =-4-5 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(-2,-9).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=2x-5.$\n\n![](images/a6/a65be51e1c9abaf82f2bd7f905936ed5550602b0fb7b5c208047684e750c3c30.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622140 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ceb9d1d-c101-5617-b68f-3fa5c94f9dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e8/e87d7c825aff9cf55a4135fc557a5bf7821c9f90bf95eb8d5c19c7cdbb5fffd6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622120} {:answer/id #uuid "6db7c9d6-81b4-55bc-86a2-dc13d77b79d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e6/e669a1b71c6456c49cc99fc11e3d56a499c8f120f36ff0dc3dd39cbe4f9c3b00.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622128} {:answer/id #uuid "830b617c-a9ed-5fb4-a2bd-e45740978958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/02615be1fd04ad3138c306723cc27f83d516e739dc7492e8fd33f31354f4a945.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622131} {:answer/id #uuid "842972be-afe3-5cba-9011-ded6815bca9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e4f94131ad0707ed469cd273bb32cf681b93a61f00893c5f918b08a1aa8abf13.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622132} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa5b314-05d0-5160-b5d3-c2433ba70490" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4e/4ef5ad32dcf50f94412bbeb8bcf083b7b7011bdc5bd60f92f9b7e43a45eaa7ad.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6db7c9d6-81b4-55bc-86a2-dc13d77b79d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e6/e669a1b71c6456c49cc99fc11e3d56a499c8f120f36ff0dc3dd39cbe4f9c3b00.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622128} :answer-field/id #uuid "a330932f-57f6-5825-b34f-9d610e9143b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d1d11299-76a9-5576-9b5e-3047d45c629a" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y=x-5?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x-5 \\\\  & =(0)-5 \\\\  & =0-5 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,-5).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x-5 \\\\  & =(2)-5 \\\\  & =2-5 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(2,-3).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=x-5.$\n\n![](images/2e/2edc9ee1cc0dd6b0b8b57d60f892146d36383e751a2226d4717fc465cbb70fd8.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622142 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bb53516-41a3-5eb8-a8d2-35ef39a022ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6b/6b133bbb0506ca855e4d6301e0140ddc3235538241c0b094677198f3472ffbb6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622114} {:answer/id #uuid "43eee2d8-4630-5b12-bbba-dcdcde9f5c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/73/73d151b1492a03c57d15c6c7270fc4cc7e14882f155f3cc506ecf9ec55105d19.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622122} {:answer/id #uuid "6e866f78-5da8-5cc1-90a1-e7f22a02b786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c4/c40f7cd1d418f16003eba614aff1a187616be908e1364198335f7d0417843720.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622129} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d20045-d55e-5096-aa13-aef653204208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9f/9f97b6ad9702c111e6046c432cdf5f79fcf4ddec9cd52d49792a6afe4e0d4bb3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622141} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd0b784-4480-556d-9382-11f7195fb650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2b/2b3b4490351bde76762a0d23b57dd74a1b93946ca2d860442a1ffd0d0c8526cd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e866f78-5da8-5cc1-90a1-e7f22a02b786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c4/c40f7cd1d418f16003eba614aff1a187616be908e1364198335f7d0417843720.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622129} :answer-field/id #uuid "314bc8ac-5f5f-59d8-9b60-cb2cfbe21e44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622115}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da768ace-dd88-5e3e-a21b-9682e66558d3" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y=-x?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-x \\\\  & =-(0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,0).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-x \\\\  & =-(1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(1,-1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-x.$ \n\n![](images/a4/a498da6031f3b5b2a67230282604884b65204b1fa6dcc2126445692729852c6c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01625a92-c861-51e4-88d3-0ada7a934e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/10/10bcfd95643b69f39bc01684e407e2e1f22ffa8b12c9585f9b63bb9e45056223.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622112} {:answer/id #uuid "3a7970f1-cd44-5dad-830f-06dc76e51754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9f/9f97b6ad9702c111e6046c432cdf5f79fcf4ddec9cd52d49792a6afe4e0d4bb3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622119} {:answer/id #uuid "65eb18f5-540e-58f2-9da7-fa4db10863f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/35/35b2711a4528df62c04203b6e0c40129d698c6c7faeee08f68bc8ce2527995b2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622126} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a2b3a4-5b36-5642-b3a0-7ff710b0eb36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0b1678ba36df87664658e4cf26a1f3fae68b1c5a427234b7a04cc96c684160d6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622135} {:answer/id #uuid "ac496907-5860-52df-bd74-9d8e6bb62415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/73/73d151b1492a03c57d15c6c7270fc4cc7e14882f155f3cc506ecf9ec55105d19.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8a2b3a4-5b36-5642-b3a0-7ff710b0eb36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0b1678ba36df87664658e4cf26a1f3fae68b1c5a427234b7a04cc96c684160d6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622135} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bfc27f0-db96-5173-86c0-07d7539845a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622123}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ebc264a6-03d6-51d7-8fa8-1d4007cbaac0" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y=4+2x?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4+2x \\\\  & =4+2(0) \\\\  & =4+0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,4).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=1.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4+2x \\\\  & =4+2(1) \\\\  & =4+2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(1,6).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=4+2x.$\n\n![](images/7a/7a3554247a7d77993c122737cd4ac3f67b12ac0745f00038f2bf9a5dd6bb77be.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff59c483-12bf-5e0b-8863-24fe707966ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff59c483-12bf-5e0b-8863-24fe707966ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622656} :answer-field/id #uuid "a87b9cd5-13c5-5cff-9489-c412d49671ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "910f989a-35f5-5b0c-8976-4bb5abd96692" :question/math-academy-id "q-317305" :question/problem "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨-\\sqrt{3},\\,-6,\\,0⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨-\\sqrt{3},\\,5,\\,9⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-\\sqrt{3},\\,-6,\\,0⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\sqrt{3},\\,5,\\,9⟩ \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{3})(-\\sqrt{3})+(-6)(5)+(0)(9) \\\\  & =3-30+0 \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622816 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3993d03c-e325-5f43-87af-9b86e1a3b93f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622408} {:answer/id #uuid "4507f1b4-c9e1-508b-86e4-1791b4db4f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622417} {:answer/id #uuid "7ddb3224-dbb4-588a-a893-758171ca72fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622495} {:answer/id #uuid "d5c011a2-24b9-5cb0-8c53-bee61ea23f16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "120" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622615} {:answer/id #uuid "ea389770-c552-518d-aaf9-48a5ce1bbb54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea389770-c552-518d-aaf9-48a5ce1bbb54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622640} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5f6e8a-1ad9-5096-95f3-660af9a7cb2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "adcbce42-edf2-574e-9d9d-79afad6b2089" :question/math-academy-id "q-128344" :question/problem "Let $p=⟨6,4,6⟩,$ $q=⟨5,0,2⟩$ and $r=⟨-1,4,-2⟩.$ Find $r\\cdot (p\\times q).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $r\\cdot (p\\times q)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $r,$ $p,$ and $q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot (p\\times q) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-4\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 6 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)(4\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 6)-4(6\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 6)-2(6\\cdot 0-5\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =-8+72+40 \\\\  & =104.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622827 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83e99952-7905-59c5-9af7-8776bd1a59cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622502} {:answer/id #uuid "96180d6f-198b-55fc-8e09-c6d0bea647f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622530} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8ba841-9b79-581f-903e-981ab3e74cea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622579} {:answer/id #uuid "cddaefa7-e4d1-55b2-9ac7-37c42636b972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622598} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf3da83-8d9f-5388-be48-50a348bb481c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cddaefa7-e4d1-55b2-9ac7-37c42636b972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622598} :answer-field/id #uuid "f23cf1ff-98d8-5cd3-b5db-ca9a1395c1fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622746}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf73151c-9dcf-51bc-b727-cf2faf814756" :question/math-academy-id "q-128354" :question/problem "Find $b\\cdot (c\\times a),$ if $b\\times c=⟨7,-2,-3⟩$ and $a=⟨1,7,5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨1,7,5⟩\\cdot ⟨7,-2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =1\\cdot 7+7\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =7-14-15 \\\\  & =-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) &=22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (c\\times a) &=-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186622835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76dee31f-49cf-50d8-8575-5fd213e31320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76dee31f-49cf-50d8-8575-5fd213e31320" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622483} :answer-field/id #uuid "a25f19c5-46b4-516f-8d46-9a16c6142ba5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186622715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f30ba5b3-3bd0-5dff-b017-f17f43501bfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-317347" :question/problem "Find $c\\cdot (a\\times b)$, if $c\\times b=⟨-4,6,3⟩$ and $a=⟨2,5,-1⟩.$\n\n$c\\cdot (a\\times b)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (c\\times b) & =⟨2,5,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,6,3⟩ \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 6+(-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-8+30-3 \\\\  & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b) &=-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186623787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9206eb63-fde8-559e-a36f-1d196016d8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623817} {:answer/id #uuid "d67cdfc2-1e96-5a43-8025-237af0303985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9206eb63-fde8-559e-a36f-1d196016d8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623817} :answer-field/id #uuid "77002078-fe3e-53ed-b8f2-d8e6466e55f0" :answer-field/key "$y=-x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623807} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f421039f-3b7c-5c05-a031-86a24684b08c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623833} {:answer/id #uuid "ffeba78d-5697-504c-9b68-bc89c0637215" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f421039f-3b7c-5c05-a031-86a24684b08c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623833} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c6c3b57-d51a-5e96-8ca1-4f1751ae62bc" :answer-field/key "$y=1-x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623818} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f11cf38-3a4d-5f8a-98bf-79b2ed9d12f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623798} {:answer/id #uuid "edc63731-f6aa-513c-bbb2-366ffd919559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "edc63731-f6aa-513c-bbb2-366ffd919559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623831} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccf4f046-a5bb-5371-9878-4c006772db05" :answer-field/key "$y+x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0a86401e-af33-5da3-93e7-d46575de5c6a" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dc355ab2667e4f215b6c7b27d00029c1c164cc054829fbc72dba82786c173810.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,1)$ and $(1,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/de/def3b4d24e1db68fbd7e872f786fa8e20e4ff4dc193ed3060c08d1b12dfd5c5e.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=-x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,1)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1) &=-(0) \\\\ 1 &=0\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-x$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=1-x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,1)$ and $B(1,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1) &=1-(0) \\\\ 1 &=1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (0) &=1-(1) \\\\ 0 &=0\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=1-x$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y+x=1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,1)$ and $B(1,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)+(0) &=1 \\\\ 1 &=1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (0)+(1) &=1 \\\\ 1 &=1\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y+x=1$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=1-x$, $y+x=1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186623792 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75612bb9-1bca-50b0-a75b-03f056b68331" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623806} {:answer/id #uuid "d8d5c8d1-01e7-5907-8d81-db4decf4b373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8d5c8d1-01e7-5907-8d81-db4decf4b373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623827} :answer-field/id #uuid "57324080-95ee-5c60-8bef-60f7125be4a5" :answer-field/key "$2y+2x=-6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623801} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44a81758-ffd0-5df8-8690-e86a98d1cfe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623794} {:answer/id #uuid "83d0d3ec-2eb5-5653-b9da-d17b2f812ee0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44a81758-ffd0-5df8-8690-e86a98d1cfe6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623794} :answer-field/id #uuid "83f38735-96ff-5b55-bb55-ba270582ef09" :answer-field/key "$y=-x-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623812} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14b164f9-63c2-500f-910f-8740566cae96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623788} {:answer/id #uuid "47d861f8-4d5d-553c-b423-8c34ddd07d12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14b164f9-63c2-500f-910f-8740566cae96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623788} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac378981-c0ed-50a5-80f9-7b72d832acf2" :answer-field/key "$y=-3+x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4083eb48-a65c-58eb-a4fb-0130fe178787" :question/problem "![](images/3d/3dcd48f167c1abd8135af4802bfe3c6abd980eba1ef2bbf0adb87156d7c2faa3.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-3)$ and $(1,-4)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/93/930d1bbba272eb5b747ebc4ece3a2b93e7509cbd1e0b58903096149854319288.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=-x-3.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(1,-4)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3) &=-(0)-3 \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-4) &=-(1)-3 \\\\ -4 &=-4\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-x-3$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $2y+2x=-6.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(1,-4)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-3)+2(0) &=-6 \\\\ -6 &=-6\\,\\checkmark \\\\ 2(-4)+2(1) &=-6 \\\\ -6 &=-6\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2y+2x=-6$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=-3+x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-3)$ and $B(1,-4)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3) &=-3+(0) \\\\ -3 &=-3\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (-4) &=-3+(1) \\\\ -4 &=-2\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-3+x$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=-x-3$, $2y+2x=-6$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186623805 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e192d527-f46e-5e91-923a-ee5995705db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623829} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f7b5ed-b7fd-5ea0-a40d-02475912a1f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e192d527-f46e-5e91-923a-ee5995705db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623829} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e840367-5b0e-5795-89f3-2c5f0d1ab2df" :answer-field/key "$y-2x=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623790} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d47021d-b7d1-59ab-b682-8deb43ed122f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623802} {:answer/id #uuid "72ae16fd-ed3e-56bb-8d06-6d7374de984e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72ae16fd-ed3e-56bb-8d06-6d7374de984e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623804} :answer-field/id #uuid "8426c3b1-f90f-5a8f-b311-217c22e9bf88" :answer-field/key "$y=2x+5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623813} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18d90508-2aec-59a1-ac0b-3e16ba2d6462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623789} {:answer/id #uuid "2ebad458-376f-5207-b7f8-6ede95c2d647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ebad458-376f-5207-b7f8-6ede95c2d647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623791} :answer-field/id #uuid "dce2a1cc-61a4-502b-9aff-3bb5f2a12c74" :answer-field/key "$y=4+2x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "73cf73d7-aed7-5537-98d4-76c7214530c3" :question/problem "![](images/76/765f4148294d78ace114858bfcd459d1eef17dd7cfcd54764b7b848b5e6acbf2.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,4)$ and $(1,6)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/16/162d47dcc98dfa30f90d511692061b524b96cac0fefa87e5db478d5cbd859b78.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=2x+5.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) &=2(0)+5 \\\\ 4 &=5\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=2x+5$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=4+2x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(1,6)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) &=4+2(0) \\\\ 4 &=4\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (6) &=4+2(1) \\\\ 6 &=6\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=4+2x$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y-2x=4.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(1,6)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4)-2(0) &=4 \\\\ 4 &=4\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (6)-2(1) &=4 \\\\ 4 &=4\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y-2x=4$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=4+2x$, $y-2x=4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186623822 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9027d197-9423-57d9-860d-4e3579b058ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623816} {:answer/id #uuid "a599de1b-4ed4-5427-ae1a-9300af4f958d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9027d197-9423-57d9-860d-4e3579b058ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623816} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a7a8189-23a7-5476-9ebf-790140dfb390" :answer-field/key "$2y-2x=-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623797} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "414d8fd7-d5c1-5871-a1ec-1045a574cb7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623793} {:answer/id #uuid "7a2aeef2-3358-53c8-9fa0-b6e3631ac134" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "414d8fd7-d5c1-5871-a1ec-1045a574cb7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623793} :answer-field/id #uuid "53a996a0-e4bb-5298-94e2-9b31110624a2" :answer-field/key "$y=-1-x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623799} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54750bae-badc-5895-80e1-30f74505032c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623800} {:answer/id #uuid "79a8bd17-9833-59d0-81f5-18aec6f4a437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79a8bd17-9833-59d0-81f5-18aec6f4a437" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623808} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbd009c5-b347-507a-ae3b-8a308ed7a802" :answer-field/key "$y=-x-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb618abc-fffb-5581-9bde-9c9323e2240e" :question/problem "![](images/da/da52fbd751e778bc191d6a7067d8bf0de81b46a1eb7db10a8af0de965c735c0e.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-1)$ and $(1,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/6c/6c23998a9dfa5ca9c3a2cfe12eafd08f2382f6006b284b04181d56c902f6c6eb.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=-x-1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(1,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) &=-(0)-1 \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (0) &=-(1)-1 \\\\ 0 &=-2\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-x-1$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $2y-2x=-2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(1,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)-2(0) &=-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ 2(0)-2(1) &=-2 \\\\ -2 &=-2\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2y-2x=-2$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=-1-x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(1,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) &=-1-(0) \\\\ -1 &=-1\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (0) &=-1-(1) \\\\ 0 &=-2\\,\\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-1-x$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $2y-2x=-2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186623832 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ccc8a83-7eca-5aee-8335-b8a82ecf2914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623815} {:answer/id #uuid "ce024f1b-5129-5f5c-ba79-e26802f71a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ccc8a83-7eca-5aee-8335-b8a82ecf2914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623815} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a97edaf-c97c-5c2c-81d8-9d17dce941c7" :answer-field/key "$y-x=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623803} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46ccedc3-ac5f-5fc4-84d1-6e8012b2dbd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623795} {:answer/id #uuid "d55b641b-f139-534f-8b88-93bbe97803f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46ccedc3-ac5f-5fc4-84d1-6e8012b2dbd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623795} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bdcaaed-df40-58aa-aaac-68e2e173e087" :answer-field/key "$y=x+2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623814} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c555e52-3d9b-59ac-aa7d-d63b3de4eb91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623810} {:answer/id #uuid "c60ff82d-d82d-5aea-87a3-88a2c42c905b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c555e52-3d9b-59ac-aa7d-d63b3de4eb91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623810} :answer-field/id #uuid "e44a2c28-cbcb-5fb9-ba4c-3b2dfdfee9b9" :answer-field/key "$y=2+x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186623830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f3ae89b4-e017-5481-a893-5525a2c4dd2d" :question/problem "![](images/80/8088eeb04d86e5719ce7b3d9f62a17a97c012107d1bff7acd9fa37c6b473ca3e.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,2)$ and $(1,3)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/d8/d8cbae503bf244e18d3ac62bc4ef87cc775e71b68e5bdab888a3c776d5080090.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=x+2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,2)$ and $B(1,3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2) &=(0)+2 \\\\ 2 &=2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (3) &=(1)+2 \\\\ 3 &=3\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=x+2$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y=2+x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,2)$ and $B(1,3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2) &=2+(0) \\\\ 2 &=2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (3) &=2+(1) \\\\ 3 &=3\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=2+x$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation: $y-x=2.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,2)$ and $B(1,3)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)-(0) &=2 \\\\ 2 &=2\\,\\checkmark \\\\ (3)-(1) &=2 \\\\ 2 &=2\\,\\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y-x=2$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nSelect $y=x+2$, $y=2+x$, $y-x=2$."}]}
